  "note": "Election of the whole council (21 members, seven for each of the North, South and West wards) on 15 January 1932. Only the West Ward was contested; North and South were filled unopposed (Irish News, 6 January 1932, p. 8; Belfast News-Letter, 16 January 1932, p. 7). The report of 8 January 1932 records no contest in the South Ward. The seven official Nationalists are listed here; Cassidy's withdrawal is inferred from the reduction from eight nominees to seven seats. Returned unopposed."
